message.content:
For a two-body decay at rest with a massless neutrino:

\[
K_\mu = \frac{(M_\pi - m_\mu)^2}{2M_\pi}
\]

\[
K_\nu = \frac{M_\pi^2 - m_\mu^2}{2M_\pi}
\]

Given:

\[
M_\pi = 139.6\ \text{MeV}, \quad m_\mu = 105.7\ \text{MeV}
\]

\[
K_\mu = \frac{(139.6 - 105.7)^2}{2(139.6)}
= \frac{33.9^2}{279.2}
\approx 4.12\ \text{MeV}
\]

\[
K_\nu = \frac{139.6^2 - 105.7^2}{279.2}
\approx 29.8\ \text{MeV}
\]

Answer: B
